-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1081, found by an independent re-check: T's deadline is at
-- 4 and its lapse arms Q's cure, 10 after it (14). `t` starts U's deadline of
-- 3, and `u` starts V's of 8, so the chain from `t` is 3 + 8 = 11 and 14 - 11 = 3
-- would be a tie for `t`. But Q's cure exists only if `t` is never done, and
-- V's deadline only if it is: the two never coexist, so no instant of `t`
-- can make them meet, and the act is not tied with the cure of its own lapse.
IMPORT prelude
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF T, U, V, Q
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF t, u, v, q

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
own MEANS
  PARTY T MUST t WITHIN 4
    HENCE (PARTY U MUST u WITHIN 3
             HENCE (PARTY V MUST v WITHIN 8 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY V)
             LEST BREACH BY U)
    LEST (PARTY Q MUST q WITHIN 10 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Q)

#TRACE own AT 0 WITH
  PARTY T DOES t AT 3
